meta {
  name: MTSS
  seq: 6
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  // Descriptors and interventions use the provider namespace; without it the API answers a
  // generic 400/403. Fail early with the fix instead.
  if (!bru.getEnvVar('providerNamespace')) {
    throw new Error('The environment has no "providerNamespace". Add it to your Sample Data environment, set to one of your API client\'s namespace prefixes (for example uri://gbisd.edu), and run this request again.');
  }
}

docs {
  # MTSS (Intervention) sample data
  
  Everything MTSS sample data needs, encapsulated so it never affects other certifications'
  sample data (SIS will get its own `SIS/Dependencies` and `SIS/Scenario Steps`).
  
  | Folder | Purpose |
  | --- | --- |
  | Dependencies | Run once, in order (Dep 1-11): our school 9999999911 under LEA 255901, students, staff, their associations, and the provider descriptors. Persistent: no down scripts. |
  | Scenario Steps | Vendor actions per certification scenario: `Step N` = the action checked by certification step N; `Sync N` = Recovery's "normal synchronization". |
  | Reset | Deletes everything the scenarios create (Down 1-13), from any state. Run it before a new pass to start from scratch; Dependencies are kept. |
  
  Values follow the Confluence certification scenarios. All creates are POSTs (natural-key
  upserts) and can be re-run. Set `providerNamespace` in the environment to one of your
  client's namespace prefixes.
}
